body:
Your backend framework wants to evaluate what's inside the js part of the code because it uses the same `{{ }}` for variables. One way to get around that is to use a function instead of a string template. Here is an example based on yours:

```js
search.addWidget(
    instantsearch.widgets.hits({
	container: '#hits',
	templates: {
	    empty: 'No results',
	    item: function(hit){ return hit.name; }
	},
	hitsPerPage: 6,
	cssClasses: {
	    root: 'row',
	    item: 'col-lg-3 col-md-4 col-sm-6'
	}
    })
);
```
